          "path": "_m/g/c/f/3/glenveagh-castle-wp/glenveagh-castle-geograph-org-.jpg",
          "filename": "Glenveagh Castle - geograph.org.uk - 51510.jpg",
          "caption": "Glenveagh Castle. Castle in Glenveagh National Park, \"along the Derryveagh mountains in the northwest of County Donegal. This 16.000 hectares of mountain, bogs, lakes and woods is cut in two by the spectacular valley of Glenveagh which gives the park its name... Lakes range in size from little hillside lochans to the majestic Lough Veagh, surrounded by the scattered remains of a forest which once covered much of Donegal.\" (from the Info Sheet of Glenveagh National Park)",
          "alt": "Glenveagh Castle. Castle in Glenveagh National Park, \"along the Derryveagh mountains in the northwest of County Donegal. This 16.000 hectares of mountain, bogs, lakes and woods is cut in two by the spectacular valley of Glenveagh which gives the park its name... Lakes range in size from little hillside lochans to the majestic Lough Veagh, surrounded by the scattered remains of a forest which once covered much of Donegal.\" (from the Info Sheet of Glenveagh National Park)",
          "width": 640,
          "height": 460,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
          "artist": "Corinna Schleiffer",
