          "filename": "Glenveagh Castle - geograph.org.uk - 51517.jpg",
          "caption": "Glenveagh Castle. \"Overlooking Lough Veagh, Glenveagh Castle stands atop a slight promontory jutting into the lake. Few buildings in Ireland can boast as fine a setting. Made from rough-hewn granite, the Castle, a castellated mansion, was built in the years 1870-73 from designs by John Townshend Trench, a cousin of John Adair.\" (From Info Sheet of Glenveagh National Park)",
          "alt": "Glenveagh Castle. \"Overlooking Lough Veagh, Glenveagh Castle stands atop a slight promontory jutting into the lake. Few buildings in Ireland can boast as fine a setting. Made from rough-hewn granite, the Castle, a castellated mansion, was built in the years 1870-73 from designs by John Townshend Trench, a cousin of John Adair.\" (From Info Sheet of Glenveagh National Park)",
